<title>HONG KONG: Lung Kee interim net rises 54 percent.</title>
<headline>Lung Kee interim net rises 54 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   18.37  vs 12.15 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0    vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    54.17  vs 35.22</p>
<p>    Turnover		     281.01 vs 212.59</p>
<p>    Company name		 Lung Kee (Bermuda) Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  Dec 30, 1996 to Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   Jan 9, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - Lung Kee makes mould bases.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted for the one-for-four bonus issue of shares allotted in September 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
